          "label": "Generative AI can support activity development, but it should support \u2014 not replace \u2014 your own instructional design, disciplinary judgment, and critical thinking. As AI plays a larger role in producing content, the expectation for your review, verification, and disclosure increases. Select the level that best describes how AI was used in developing this activity.\n\u2022 <b>Routine or Supportive use</b> covers things like brainstorming, wording suggestions, grammar/clarity checks, or formatting on work you conceived and directed.\n\u2022 <b>Substantive Developmental use</b> means AI helped develop or revise real components \u2014 drafting objectives, generating questions from your objectives, building datasets, or suggesting scaffolding \u2014 requiring your careful review and verification.\n\u2022 <b>Extensive Generative use</b> means AI generated substantial portions of the activity (e.g. a full question sequence or draft) with limited initial input from you.",
